# One tote project, two hostnames (do not mix with splash)

| URL | Project | Tree | What it is |
|---|---|---|---|
| **https://ngmi.markets** | `ngmi-stage` (`prj_CAYYd91QDAJvDJSwLDPWnGN5gfRb`) | `/tmp/ngmi-stage` + `apps/web` | Next.js tote. Title **NGMI**. |
| **https://ngmi-stage.vercel.app** | same `ngmi-stage` | same | Same tote. Title **NGMI staging**. |
| splash project `ngmi` (`prj_RVPkHN5tGZFTCrte7DMZMMrkiMp0`) | `apps/landing` | Parked. Do not point `ngmi.markets` at it. |

If `ngmi.markets` title is the splash line (**NGMI — over the mark before T**), landing stole the domain. Move `ngmi.markets` / `www.ngmi.markets` back onto `ngmi-stage` and redeploy the tote. Never `vercel --name ngmi-stage` from `apps/landing`. Never `vercel link` landing to `ngmi-stage`. Never set this project's root to `apps/landing`. `git.deploymentEnabled` is false on the tote.

## Tote deploy

After any `apps/web` change, deploy **ngmi-stage** before saying the work is done. `apps/web` stays gitignored. That production deploy is what `ngmi.markets` serves.

Sync into `/tmp/ngmi-stage` (keep `.vercel` and `.env.local`). Workspace yaml in that tree **must** include `apps/web`. Root directory `apps/web`, framework `nextjs`. Then:

```
npx --yes vercel@latest deploy --prod --yes --cwd /tmp/ngmi-stage --scope frsr --logs
```

Splash folder deploys (`pnpm deploy` in `apps/landing`) stay on project `ngmi` only — never `--force` those domains onto `ngmi`.
